menu "Opus ESP32-P4 kernels"

choice OPUS_P4_KERNEL_MODE
    prompt "Opus kernel implementation"
    default OPUS_P4_KERNEL_PORTABLE

    config OPUS_P4_KERNEL_PORTABLE
        bool "Portable C"

    config OPUS_P4_KERNEL_ASM
        bool "ESP32-P4 asm ABI scaffold"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            Route implemented kernel boundaries through their P4 assembly
            symbols. The anti-collapse noise symbol is currently an ABI
            scaffold that tail-calls the portable C reference.

    config OPUS_P4_KERNEL_ASM_VERIFY
        bool "ESP32-P4 asm ABI scaffold with C verification"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            Verify the first calls against the portable C contract and latch
            a permanent C fallback on any mismatch. The anti-collapse noise
            symbol is currently an ABI scaffold, not an optimized PIE kernel.
endchoice

config OPUS_P4_VERIFY_CALLS
    int "Calls verified before accepting an asm kernel"
    default 64
    range 1 4096
    depends on OPUS_P4_KERNEL_ASM_VERIFY
    help
        Number of calls checked before a kernel changes from verification to
        direct asm dispatch for the rest of the boot.

config OPUS_P4_FUNCTION_PROFILE
    bool "Instrument Opus functions for profiling"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
    help
        Add compiler function instrumentation to esp_opus_float and collect
        approximate per-function self cycles during the boot benchmark.
        Enable only for profiling builds because the overhead is substantial.

endmenu
